Delete:
Delete is the Data manipulation language command. It is used to remove specific rows or all rows from a table.
(1) Remove rows one by one.
(2) can be rolled back using a transaction.
(3) Supports the WHERE clause.


Truncate:
Truncate is a Data definition language command. It is used to remove all records from a table quickly.
(1) Remove all rows at once.
(2) Can be rolled back using a transaction.
(3) Does not support the WHERE clause.


Drop:
DROP is a Data definition language command. It is used to permanently database objects such as tables, views, database, SP.
(1) Remove both data and table structure.
(2) Can be rolled back using a transaction.



